E-Commerce Data Cleaning & Preparation
A practical data cleaning and preparation project using PostgreSQL and SQL on a relational e-commerce dataset. The project demonstrates how raw business data can be inspected, validated, standardized, and prepared for downstream analytics.

Project Objective
The objective is to identify common data-quality issues in raw e-commerce data and produce reliable datasets ready for SQL analysis, exploratory analysis, and BI dashboards.

Dataset Overview
The project contains 7 related datasets:

Table                 Description

Customers       Customer identifiers and location

Orders          Order details, status, and dates

Order Items     Products and sellers associated with orders

Payments        Payment methods, installments, and values

Reviews         Customer ratings and review information

Products        Product attributes and categories

Sellers         Seller identifiers and location

Data Quality Checks    
*The cleaning process focuses on five key areas:
*Missing values — identify NULL and empty values in important fields
*Duplicate records — detect repeated business records using relevant identifiers
*Incorrect data types — validate and convert dates and numeric fields
*Inconsistent values — standardize text such as cities, states, statuses, and payment types
*Invalid values — validate business rules such as review scores and non-negative monetary values

Cleaning Methodology
The PostgreSQL workflow follows:
Raw Data → Data Profiling → Quality Checks → Cleaning & Standardization → Validation → Cleaned Data

SQL functions and techniques include:
TRIM()
LOWER()
UPPER()
INITCAP()
DISTINCT
NULL checks
Data type conversion
Business-rule validation

